WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:06.340
Faux ribbing is a tuck stitch pattern
that resembles ribbing on the knit side.

2
00:00:06.370 --> 00:00:12.780
It's not stretchy like ribbing, it just
mimics the texture of 2x1 ribbing.

3
00:00:12.810 --> 00:00:15.380
I'm showing the stitch pattern on a manual

4
00:00:15.410 --> 00:00:20.500
machine using the hold setting. But it can
also be worked on an automatic patterning

5
00:00:20.530 --> 00:00:26.140
machine with this stitch
pattern and the tuck setting.

6
00:00:26.170 --> 00:00:29.140
I've started my stitch pattern and you can

7
00:00:29.170 --> 00:00:36.340
see that these needles have tucked and
there are strands over the held needles.

8
00:00:36.370 --> 00:00:38.520
Now take the flat edge of your needle

9
00:00:38.550 --> 00:00:43.660
pusher and push those needles
back into middle position.

10
00:00:43.680 --> 00:00:50.340
Use the 2x2 needle pusher again and
push the opposite needles to hold.

11
00:00:50.370 --> 00:00:55.760
Make sure you are not
holding the edge stitches.

12
00:00:56.160 --> 00:01:01.980
Knit across and notice the
strands now over those needles.

13
00:01:02.010 --> 00:01:04.540
Repeat this for the pattern

14
00:01:04.570 --> 00:01:13.740
hold sets of two needles, knit across,
alternate the sets of needles and tuck.

15
00:01:13.770 --> 00:01:18.100
Making sure you aren't
tucking the end needles.

16
00:01:18.130 --> 00:01:25.140
Remember this is tuck and tuck
requires more weight than stockinette.

17
00:01:25.170 --> 00:01:27.260
Be sure to watch your knitting to make

18
00:01:27.290 --> 00:01:31.920
sure that the stitches are
knitting off correctly.

19
00:01:35.120 --> 00:01:38.290
I encourage you to to give
this one a try for yourself.

20
00:01:38.320 --> 00:01:40.820
It's a little hard to see in the photos

21
00:01:40.850 --> 00:01:47.780
but it has great texture and the purl side
is quite attractive and textured as well.

22
00:01:47.800 --> 00:01:48.960
I hope you'll give it a try.

